## 3. Stage-by-Stage Mint-to Logic™ & Shepherd's Process Analysis

* **`[100]` Intake & Host/Session Boundary Normalization:** Normalizes incoming agent/client requests and local host traffic across network/firewall rules, identity/session tokens, and execution entrypoints.
* **`[200]` Validation / Firewall Allowlist, Token & Policy Checks:** Enforces host firewall rules, identity/JWT validation, and policy gates before permitting traffic or tool execution—acting as a boundary check rather than a per-unit mint trigger.
* **`[300]` Mint Unit / Isolated MicroVM & Session State Context:** Isolates each session's CPU, memory, filesystem, and runtime context inside a dedicated sandbox/microVM—providing strong session-level isolation without sealing a cryptographic Mint Unit Container with hash, timestamp, routing directive, and commit fields.
* **`[400]` Routing / Session Dispatch & Compute Scaling:** Routes requests into dedicated session environments and manages compute scaling/placement across active vs. idle states—mirroring operational dispatch without branching a unit into Burn, Limbo, Access, or Code protocol states.
* **`[500a]` Burn / Session Tear-Down & Idle Memory Reclamation:** Reclaims memory and tears down idle or completed sessions—providing resource reclamation and cleanup rather than an authorization-gated single-use credential burn on a discrete mint unit.
* **`[500b]` Limbo / Throttling, Rate Limits & Session Holds:** Applies per-session counters, rate limits, and connection/execution holds when concurrency or policy thresholds are reached—without a full dual escalation/re-routing branch and expiration/auto-burn timer on a mint unit.
* **`[500c]` Access / Firewall Allow-Listing & Isolated Per-Session Boundaries:** Combines host firewall allow-listing with isolated per-session compute/storage/network boundaries to prevent cross-session leakage and unauthorized reach.
* **`[500d]` Code / Sandboxed Code, Browser & Tool Execution:** Executes code, terminal commands, browser actions, and tools inside isolated session sandboxes rather than directly on unprotected host state.
* **`[600]` Audit / Security Logs, Telemetry & Session Traces:** Records authorization outcomes, security/firewall/runtime events, and observability telemetry—supporting operational and security auditing rather than a dedicated Mint-to Logic compliance ledger.

